# PART 5 — UNIQUE PAYMENT ID GENERATION

This is a critical requirement.

## 5.1 Payment Request ID vs Payment ID

Design the system with separate identifiers.

**Payment Request ID:** Represents an amount due against a particular invoice or instalment.

**Payment ID:** Represents an individual payment attempt initiated by a customer.

When the customer deliberately initiates a new payment attempt, the backend generates a new unique Payment ID.

Example:

Customer ID: FXC-0045

Invoice ID: FXINV-0102

Payment Request ID: FXREQ-2026-0042

First Payment ID: FXPAY-2026-A81F

Second Payment ID: FXPAY-2026-B93K

Even when both attempts relate to the same advance invoice, they must have different Payment IDs.

Store internal UUIDs as primary keys and generate unique, human-readable public references.

Enforce database uniqueness.

### Duplicate Click Protection

The client may double-click Pay Now or experience network retries.

Implement idempotency keys to ensure accidental duplicate requests do not create unwanted payment attempts.

An intentional new retry may generate a separate Payment ID.

### Banking Reference

The UPI network may generate a separate UTR or transaction reference.

This external bank reference must be stored independently of the ForgeX-generated Payment ID.

Never assume they are identical.

