# PART 9 — MISSING PAYMENT AND DISPUTE SYSTEM

Create a Missing Payment button within the customer's payment details screen.

The customer should be able to provide:

- Associated Payment ID (automatically linked)
- UPI transaction reference
- Amount they claim to have paid
- Approximate transaction time
- Optional explanation

The system creates a support/verification ticket.

A customer-provided screenshot may be accepted as supporting information, but it must never be treated as conclusive payment evidence.

Finance HQ receives a notification.

Finance admins may:

- Assign the ticket
- Request clarification
- Check bank records
- Record a matching bank credit
- Approve after verification
- Reject with a reason
- Reopen the investigation

Notify the customer whenever the ticket status changes.

Apply reasonable limits to duplicate dispute submissions.

